Great! Here’s a list of the most commonly used primary functions and properties in a Pandas *DataFrame (df)*, grouped by purpose so you can learn them efficiently:

---

📄 1. Basic Info & Structure

| Function/Property       | Purpose                          |
|--------------------------|----------------------------------|
| df.shape              | Rows and columns (tuple)         |
| df.columns            | List of column names             |
| df.index              | Index (row labels)               |
| df.dtypes             | Data types of each column        |
| df.info()             | Summary of DataFrame structure   |
| df.describe()         | Stats summary (mean, std, etc.)  |
| df.head(n)            | First n rows                     |
| df.tail(n)            | Last n rows                      |

---

📊 2. Selecting & Accessing Data

| Function/Property       | Purpose                          |
|--------------------------|----------------------------------|
| df['col'] or df.col | Select single column             |
| df[['col1', 'col2']]  | Select multiple columns          |
| df.loc[row, col]      | Access by label              |
| df.iloc[row, col]     | Access b| df.at[row, col]       | Fast access for scalar value     |
| df.iat[row, col]      | Fast access by position          |

---

🔍 3. Filtering & Conditions

python
df[df['price'] > 10000]      # Rows where condition is True
df[df['brand'] == 'BMW']     # Filter by value
df[(df['price'] > 10000) & (df['mileage'] < 20)]


---

🔄 4. Modifying Data

| Function                  | Purpose                          |
|---------------------------|----------------------------------|
| df['new'] = ...         | Add a new column                 |
| df.drop(columns=['col'])| Drop column                      |
| df.drop(index=3)        | Drop row by index                |
| df.rename(columns={})   | Rename columns                   |
| df.sort_values('col')   | Sort by column                   |
| df.reset_index()        | Reset row index                  |
| df.set_index('col')     | Set a column as index            |

---

📈 5. Aggregation & Grouping

| Function                    | Purpose                        |
|-----------------------------|--------------------------------|
| df.sum()                  | Sum by column                  |
| df.mean()                 | Mean by column                 || df.groupby('col')         | Group by column                |
| .agg(['mean', 'max'])     | Multiple aggregations          |
| df['col'].value_counts()  | Frequency count                |
| df['col'].unique()        | Unique values                  |

---

🧹 6. Handling Missing Data

| Function                  | Purpose                          |
|---------------------------|----------------------------------|
| df.isnull()             | Detect missing values            |
| df.notnull()            | Detect non-missing values        |
| df.dropna()             | Drop rows with missing data      |
| df.fillna(value)        | Fill missing values              |

---
💾 7. Input & Output

| Function                  | Purpose                          |
|---------------------------|----------------------------------|
| pd.read_csv('file.csv') | Read CSV                         |
| df.to_csv('file.csv')   | Save DataFrame to CSV            |
| df.to_excel('file.xlsx')| Export to Excel                  |

